            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report on a 46-year-old man with vasospastic angina. The differential diagnosis, the eventful course of the patient and in particular the clinical image with diagnostic approach, therapy and prognosis of vasospastic angina are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
